---
description: Payday testing standards — naming, selectors, isolation, money assertions
alwaysApply: true
---

Always-on standards for this repo. `AGENTS.md` holds the full version; this file is the
Cursor dialect and must not contradict it.

- Test names: `should [expected behavior] when [condition]`.
- Selector priority: `getByTestId` > `getByRole` > semantic CSS. Never XPath.
- Every test clears localStorage in `beforeEach`, then reloads. No shared state.
- Auto-waiting assertions only. **Never `page.waitForTimeout()`.**
- One logical assertion per test. Arrange–Act–Assert with comments.
- Money assertions compare whole formatted strings (`'267.522 kr.'`), never parsed floats.
- Read `main.js` before asserting behaviour. Do not infer it from test names.
- When a test fails, state explicitly whether the test is stale or the app is wrong.
